---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import { ArrowDownToLine, ArrowRight, ArrowUpRight, CirclePlay } from '@lucide/astro';

const site = 'https://github.com/loftwah/prints-desktop';
const version = '0.3.1';
const release = `${site}/releases/tag/v${version}`;
const downloadRoot = `${site}/releases/download/v${version}/prints-desktop-${version}`;
const asset = '/prints-desktop/';
const afterlight = `${asset}afterlight-native-v0.3.1.webp`;
const local = `${asset}local-library-v0.3.1.webp`;
const hosted = `${asset}oyster-library-demo-v0.3.1.webp`;
const builds = [
  { label: 'macOS', detail: 'Apple Silicon · macOS 14+', file: 'macos-arm64.zip' },
  { label: 'Linux', detail: 'x64 · Portable archive', file: 'linux-x64.tar.gz' },
  { label: 'Linux', detail: 'ARM64 · Portable archive', file: 'linux-arm64.tar.gz' },
  { label: 'Windows', detail: 'x64 · Portable ZIP', file: 'windows-x64.zip' },
];
---

<Base
  title="Prints Desktop"
  description="A native workspace for browsing images, shortlisting favourites and keeping the originals. Explore the offline Afterlight collection or connect your private Prints library through Oyster."
  shareImage={`${asset}prints-desktop-share-v0.3.1.jpg`}
  shareAlt="Prints Desktop beside The Last Horizon, an orange sun inside a concrete ring over a volcanic coast."
>
  <article class="prints">
    <header class="prints-hero">
      <div>
        <img class="prints-mark" src={`${asset}aperture-96.png`} width="56" height="56" alt="" />
        <h1>Prints Desktop</h1>
        <p class="hero-description">A native workspace for images worth keeping. Look closer, shortlist your favourites and take the original files with you.</p>
      </div>
      <nav class="hero-actions" aria-label="Get Prints Desktop">
        <a class="download" href="#downloads"><ArrowDownToLine size={19} aria-hidden="true" /> Get the desktop app</a>
        <a class="quiet-link" href="#walkthrough"><CirclePlay size={19} aria-hidden="true" /> Watch the walkthrough</a>
      </nav>
    </header>

    <figure class="workspace">
      <a href={afterlight} aria-label="Open the Afterlight workspace screenshot at full size">
        <img src={afterlight} width="1440" height="880" alt="Prints Desktop shows a concrete ring and orange sun in The Last Horizon, with six studies in the contact sheet and the selected print’s brief in the inspector." fetchpriority="high" decoding="async" />
      </a>
      <figcaption><strong>Afterlight</strong><span>Six original studies bundled with the app. Available offline on first launch.</span></figcaption>
    </figure>

    <section class="editorial" aria-labelledby="what-title">
      <h2 id="what-title">A place to decide what stays.</h2>
      <div class="editorial-copy">
        <p>Prints Desktop gives a collection the room it deserves. The contact sheet keeps the sequence in view. Open a print at full size, read its brief, or return to the ideas you’ve starred.</p>
        <p>It began with a simple problem. The image you want to keep can get buried between a generation history, a download folder and a draft. Prints puts those decisions in a native workspace and lets you export the original bytes.</p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="tour" id="walkthrough" aria-labelledby="walkthrough-title">
      <div class="tour-heading">
        <h2 id="walkthrough-title">From first look to export.</h2>
        <p>Watch the native app browse Afterlight, save an original, draft a prompt and open an example Oyster library.</p>
      </div>
      <figure>
        <video controls playsinline preload="none" poster={afterlight} aria-label="Prints Desktop walkthrough">
          <source src={`${asset}prints-desktop-walkthrough-v0.3.1.mp4`} type="video/mp4" />
          <track kind="captions" label="English" srclang="en" src={`${asset}prints-desktop-walkthrough-v0.3.1.en.vtt`} default />
        </video>
        <figcaption>28 seconds · Silent, with captions · Native Rune capture</figcaption>
      </figure>
      <details>
        <summary>Read the walkthrough</summary>
        <ol>
          <li>Open Afterlight and select <cite>Blue Hour</cite> from the contact sheet. View it at full size.</li>
          <li>Add the study to Favourites, return to it and export the bundled JPEG.</li>
          <li>Copy the creative brief from <cite>The Last Horizon</cite> into an editable prompt draft and save it locally.</li>
          <li>Browse a folder and preview a print in a connected Oyster library seeded with fictional media.</li>
        </ol>
      </details>
    </section>

    <section class="workflows" aria-labelledby="workflows-title">
      <h2 id="workflows-title">Two ways into the workspace.</h2>
      <div class="workflow">
        <div>
          <h3>Start with your own files.</h3>
          <p>Bring in a JPEG, PNG or WebP. Linked originals and their favourites reopen after you quit. If an original moves, locate it again from the inspector.</p>
          <p>Afterlight, local imports and saved drafts work on your device without an account or model credits.</p>
        </div>
        <figure class="workspace">
          <a href={local} aria-label="Open the local imports screenshot at full size">
            <img src={local} width="1010" height="690" alt="Local imports shows Blue Hour Study, a blue mountain landscape, with eight linked images in the contact sheet." loading="lazy" decoding="async" />
          </a>
          <figcaption><strong>Local imports</strong><span>Example files linked on this device.</span></figcaption>
        </figure>
      </div>
      <div class="workflow">
        <div>
          <h3>Connect a Prints library.</h3>
          <p>Enter your Oyster origin, Prints installation ID and a named read key scoped to that installation. Browse indexed output, inspect prompts and export originals. Folder and model discovery depend on the host.</p>
          <p><strong>Create in web Prints</strong> opens the upstream app for generation. The desktop can remember your read key in your system credential store.</p>
          <a class="quiet-link" href={`${site}/blob/v${version}/docs/oyster.md`}>Read the connection guide <ArrowUpRight size={16} aria-hidden="true" /></a>
        </div>
        <figure class="workspace">
          <a href={hosted} aria-label="Open the example hosted library screenshot at full size">
            <img src={hosted} width="1440" height="880" alt="The connected Prints library previews a ring at dusk alongside folder selection, model details, and an Export original button." loading="lazy" decoding="async" />
          </a>
          <figcaption><strong>Prints library</strong><span>Native capture using a fictional Oyster library.</span></figcaption>
        </figure>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="editorial ecosystem" aria-labelledby="ecosystem-title">
      <div>
        <h2 id="ecosystem-title">How the pieces fit.</h2>
        <p>Each project has a job. The workspace, the host, the media and the showcase keep their own roles.</p>
      </div>
      <dl>
        <div>
          <dt>Prints Desktop</dt>
          <dd>Loftwah’s independent Rust and Rune app. It runs the offline workspace and talks directly to Oyster for supported, authorised reads.</dd>
        </div>
        <div>
          <dt><a href="https://docs.fungi.computer/oyster">Oyster</a> and <a href="https://docs.fungi.computer/apps/prints">Prints</a></dt>
          <dd>Oyster hosts the Fungi app and checks access to the installation and selected Computer. Prints keeps its library index, prompts and media metadata alongside the originals saved on that Computer.</dd>
        </div>
        <div>
          <dt><a href="https://docs.fungi.computer/apps/prints#store-generated-images-in-r2-from-a-durable-object">Darkroom</a></dt>
          <dd>Fungi’s generation and recovery layer. When you create through web Prints, the host and selected model determine availability, storage and charges.</dd>
        </div>
        <div>
          <dt><a href="/projects">App Composer</a></dt>
          <dd>The public home for the project, its walkthrough and downloads. The desktop project ships from its own repository.</dd>
        </div>
      </dl>
    </section>

    <section class="editorial releases" id="downloads" aria-labelledby="downloads-title">
      <div>
        <h2 id="downloads-title">Take the workspace with you.</h2>
        <p>v{version} preview. Extract the archive for your platform, then open Prints Desktop.</p>
        <a class="quiet-link" href={release}>Release notes, signing status and checksums <ArrowUpRight size={16} aria-hidden="true" /></a>
      </div>
      <div>
        <ul class="builds" aria-label="Platform downloads">
          {builds.map(({ label, detail, file }) => (
            <li>
              <a href={`${downloadRoot}-${file}`}>
                <span><strong>{label}</strong><span>{detail}</span></span>
                <ArrowDownToLine size={20} aria-hidden="true" />
              </a>
            </li>
          ))}
        </ul>
        <p class="release-note">The Mac preview is ad-hoc signed and unnotarised. macOS may block it when opened from a web download. See the release notes for platform verification.</p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <footer class="prints-credit">
      <p>Built by Loftwah with Rust and Anomaly’s Rune. Afterlight is original ImageGen artwork. Oyster, Prints and Darkroom are projects from Fungi.</p>
      <div>
        <a class="quiet-link" href={site}>Source on GitHub <ArrowUpRight size={16} aria-hidden="true" /></a>
        <a class="quiet-link" href="https://github.com/loftwah/app-composer/issues/1292">Follow the build <ArrowRight size={16} aria-hidden="true" /></a>
      </div>
    </footer>
  </article>
</Base>

<style>
  .prints {
    --prints-accent: #ffb08c;
    --prints-screen: #19151f;
    --prints-rule: var(--color-border);
  }

  :global([data-theme="light"]) .prints { --prints-accent: #96371e; }
  .prints :is(section, details) { scroll-margin-top: 5rem; }
  .prints-hero {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1fr) auto;
    align-items: end;
    gap: 22px 48px;
    padding: clamp(15px, 3vw, 43px) 0 clamp(25px, 4vw, 42px);
  }

  .prints-mark { display: block; margin-left: -5px; width: 52px; height: 52px; }
  .prints h1 {
    margin: 9px 0 13px;
    max-width: none;
    font-size: clamp(3rem, 8.5vw, 6rem);
    font-weight: 625;
    line-height: 1;
    letter-spacing: -.04em;
    text-wrap: balance;
  }

  .hero-description {
    max-width: 50ch;
    margin: 0;
    color: var(--color-muted);
    font-size: clamp(1.03rem, 1.9vw, 1.24rem);
    text-wrap: pretty;
  }

  .hero-actions { display: grid; justify-items: start; gap: 5px; }
  .download, .quiet-link { display: inline-flex; align-items: center; gap: 9px; min-height: 44px; }
  .download { justify-content: center; padding: 10px 15px; border-radius: 8px; color: #20151c; background: #ffc3a7; font-weight: 650; }
  .download:hover { background: #ffae88; }
  .quiet-link, .ecosystem dt a { color: var(--prints-accent); }
  .quiet-link:hover, .ecosystem dt a:hover { color: var(--color-foreground); }
  .prints :is(a, summary):focus-visible { outline: 2px solid var(--prints-accent); outline-offset: 4px; }

  .prints figure { margin: 0; }
  .workspace a { display: block; border-radius: 12px; }
  .workspace img, .tour video {
    display: block;
    width: 100%;
    height: auto;
    border: 1px solid var(--prints-rule);
    border-radius: 12px;
    background: var(--prints-screen);
  }

  .prints figcaption { display: flex; flex-wrap: wrap; gap: 2px 13px; margin-top: 9px; color: var(--color-muted); font-size: .88rem; }
  .prints figcaption strong { color: var(--color-foreground); }
  .prints section { margin-top: clamp(45px, 7vw, 92px); }
  .prints h2 { margin: 0 0 12px; font-size: clamp(1.8rem, 4vw, 3.2rem); line-height: 1.08; letter-spacing: -.03em; text-wrap: balance; }
  .prints h3 { margin: 0 0 10px; font-size: clamp(1.32rem, 2.5vw, 2rem); line-height: 1.18; letter-spacing: -.02em; }
  .prints p:not(.hero-description) { margin: 0 0 .8em; color: var(--color-muted); max-width: 69ch; text-wrap: pretty; }
  .editorial, .workflow, .tour-heading { display: grid; grid-template-columns: minmax(0, .74fr) minmax(0, 1.26fr); gap: 14px clamp(25px, 6vw, 76px); align-items: start; }
  .editorial { border-top: 1px solid var(--prints-rule); padding-top: clamp(20px, 4vw, 40px); }
  .editorial-copy p { font-size: clamp(1rem, 1.6vw, 1.16rem); }
  .tour { border-top: 1px solid var(--prints-rule); padding-top: clamp(20px, 4vw, 40px); }
  .tour-heading { margin-bottom: 15px; }
  .tour video { aspect-ratio: 18 / 11; }
  .tour details { margin-top: 13px; color: var(--color-muted); }
  .tour summary { display: list-item; width: fit-content; min-height: 44px; align-content: center; color: var(--prints-accent); cursor: pointer; }
  .tour ol { max-width: 70ch; padding-inline-start: 1.35rem; margin: 3px 0 0; }
  .tour li + li { margin-top: 7px; }

  .workflows > h2 { margin-bottom: 19px; }
  .workflow { border-top: 1px solid var(--prints-rule); padding-top: clamp(18px, 3vw, 29px); }
  .workflow + .workflow { margin-top: clamp(28px, 4vw, 48px); }
  .ecosystem dl { margin: 0; }
  .ecosystem dl div { display: grid; grid-template-columns: minmax(125px, .52fr) minmax(0, 1.48fr); gap: 7px 14px; padding: 12px 0; border-top: 1px solid var(--prints-rule); }
  .ecosystem dt { font-weight: 650; }
  .ecosystem dd { margin: 0; color: var(--color-muted); }
  .builds { list-style: none; padding: 0; margin: 0 0 12px; }
  .builds li { border-top: 1px solid var(--prints-rule); }
  .builds li:last-child { border-bottom: 1px solid var(--prints-rule); }
  .builds a { display: flex; justify-content: space-between; align-items: center; min-height: 60px; gap: 10px; padding: 7px 4px; color: var(--prints-accent); }
  .builds a > span { display: flex; align-items: baseline; flex-wrap: wrap; gap: 2px 13px; }
  .builds a span span { color: var(--color-muted); font-size: .9rem; }
  .builds a:hover strong { text-decoration: underline; }
  .release-note, .prints-credit { font-size: .9rem; }
  .prints-credit { display: flex; justify-content: space-between; flex-wrap: wrap; align-items: baseline; gap: 6px 21px; margin-top: clamp(28px, 5vw, 56px); padding-top: 17px; border-top: 1px solid var(--prints-rule); }
  .prints-credit div { display: flex; flex-wrap: wrap; gap: 4px 17px; }

  @media (max-width: 760px) {
    .prints-hero, .editorial, .workflow, .tour-heading { grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1fr); }
    .hero-actions { grid-template-columns: auto 1fr; align-items: center; gap: 9px 15px; }
    .prints h1 { font-size: clamp(2.9rem, 10vw, 4.8rem); }
    .ecosystem dl div { grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1fr); }
    .tour-heading { gap: 0; }
  }

  @media (max-width: 455px) {
    .hero-actions { grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1fr); gap: 4px; }
  }
</style>
